-- title:
--   Disc laws at affine readings on the Deligne–Rapoport model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that becomes $1$ modulo $M/p$, and $hj$ asserting that $jqModC \mathbb{Q}$ lies in $qExpFunctionFieldC \mathbb{Q} \top$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a datum of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, residue field $\kappa$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R p \to A$ lifting the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Further data: a unit $pb$ of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ reducing to $p$; the map $\delta$ on places of $Fbar = qExpFunctionFieldC \kappa (\Gamma_N)$ given by the semilinear action of the diamond automorphism $diamondActionModL$ at the $\Gamma_0$-lift of $pb$; a finset $SS$ whose members are exactly the pairs in $ssNodePairsQExp$; an automorphism $\theta$ of $F_M = xHFunctionFieldBar M H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map $\alpha : xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup\,p\,M\,H) \to F_M$ with $\theta \circ \alpha$ integral and $\alpha$ the identity on Laurent coefficients; a specialization $Psp$ of places with a prolongation datum $Rpd$ for $\theta$, satisfying the type dichotomy and the model laws $IsModel$; a $\theta$-equivariance property $hwgen$ of $\mathfrak{X}$'s points; and two compatibility tables $hcompat$, $hcompat'$ identifying, for $i \in \{0,1\}$, the place attached to a closed point of the $i$-th component of the special fibre with $Psp.reduceFst\,\alpha$ or $Psp.reduceSnd\,(\theta \circ \alpha)\,\delta$ of the place of a generic point, respectively with its $\delta$- and Frobenius-twisted counterparts (hypotheses summarised here). The conclusion is the conjunction of two disc laws, one for each kind. In the first: whenever $Q \neq Q'$ are places of $F_M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, both $IsStrictFst$ for $(\alpha, \theta \circ \alpha, \delta)$, with $Psp.reduceFst\,\alpha\,Q' = Psp.reduceFst\,\alpha\,Q$ and this common place affine in the sense of $IsAffinePlace$ (it assigns a value to an element whose Laurent expansion is $jqModC \kappa$), $n$ is a natural number with nonzero image in $\kappa$, $g$ lies in the integers of $Rpd.R_1$ with nonzero residue and satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_Q g = -n$, $\operatorname{ord}_{Q'} g = n$ and $\operatorname{ord}_W g = 0$ for every other strict place $W$ of the first kind with the same reduction, and $g = 1 + e\,\varepsilon$ with $e \in A$ and $\varepsilon$ in the integers of $Rpd.R_1$ of nonzero residue, then the order of the residue of $\varepsilon$ at $Psp.reduceFst\,\alpha\,Q$ is at least $-1$. The second law is the same statement with $IsStrictSnd$, $Psp.reduceSnd\,(\theta \circ \alpha)\,\delta$ and $Rpd.R_2$ in place of their first-kind counterparts.
--
--   These are the two "disc laws" bounding below the order of the reduced parameter $\bar\varepsilon$ at an affine reading of a pair of colliding strict places, proved from the Deligne–Rapoport integral model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$ together with the prolongation and specialization data. They are exactly the inputs required by the downstream assembly results on glued specializations, component groups and the vanishing of the relevant kernel, namely [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_jHPlaceSpecialization_prolongationDatum_gluedSpecialization_componentGroup_offDiag_of_wgen`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_jHPlaceSpecialization_prolongationDatum_gluedSpecialization_componentGroup_offDiag_of_wgen) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_pic0Mk_eq_forall_isStrict_or_reduceFst_mem_of_prolongationDatum_offDiag_of_wgen`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_pic0Mk_eq_forall_isStrict_or_reduceFst_mem_of_prolongationDatum_offDiag_of_wgen).
